# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To obtain or secure a copyright for some literary or other artistic work.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907 |title=District of Columbia Appropriations|author=United States Congress House. Committee on Appropriations |page=253 |ISBN= |passage= Every book will be '''copyrighted''' that the publisher believes will have such a market as will justify him in going to the expense of '''copyrighting''' to prevent competition from other publishers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993 |title=The Beast at Work|author=Gyeorgos Ceres Hatonn |page=161 |ISBN=156935006X |passage=Further, Mr. Mullins writes FOR YOU-THE-PEOPLE, '''copyrighting''' to protect listings and to make a statement—but willingly shares his work for, after all, if it is not read then of what worth is a book? }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997 |title=All Area Access: Personal Management for Unsigned Musicians |author=Marc Davison |page=171 |ISBN=0793581346 |passage=The sealed contents inside postmarked by the United States Post office will be proof enough of exactly when your work was completed. The disadvantage to this form of '''copyrighting''' is that your work is not traceable for anyone who is interested in acquiring information regarding copyright ownership. }}
#* '''2002''', ''{{w|Spider-Man (2002 film)|Spider-Man}}'' (film)
#*: J. J. Jameson: The Green Goblin. You like that? Made it up myself. These weirdos all gotta have a name now. Hoffman! Call the patent office, '''copyright''' the name "Green Goblin". I want a quarter every time somebody says it.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006 |title=The Complete Guide to Low-Budget Feature Filmmaking|author=Josh Becker; Bruce Campbell |page=55 |ISBN=0809556901 |passage=When your script is completed you need to '''copyright''' it with the Library of Congress in Washington DC (you can get the forms from: Register of Copyrights, Library of Congress, Washington DC, 20559. Request form PA, or you can download them from www.loc.gov/copyright). }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008 |title=Don't Steal Copyrighted Stuff!|author=Ann Gaines |page= |ISBN=0766028615 |passage=Everything else that is written or created is automatically '''copyrighted'''. }}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal|nonstandard}} To [[flag]] for copyright violation, to [[copystrike]].
#: {{ux|en|I won’t play this track, I don’t wanna get '''copyrighted'''.}}

